# Everything, then the handful of paths the build actually reads. An allowlist rather than a
# denylist: the failure mode of a denylist here is a secret or a 2GB cache entering the context
# because nobody remembered to add a line for it.
*
!pyproject.toml
!policy.yaml
!policy.schema.json
!src/
!docs/
!corpus/
!tools/
!streamlit_app.py
!.streamlit/config.toml

# `tests/` is excluded above and stays excluded, with one exception. Replay is the only provider
# this image can use and it reads `tests/cassettes/`, so the cassettes are runtime data that
# happens to live under a test directory. Nothing else from `tests/` is in the image.
!tests/cassettes/

# Re-excluded inside the allowed trees. Generated or machine-local, and `corpus/fixtures/` in
# particular is regenerated rather than committed.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
corpus/fixtures/

# Never, under any allowlist. A key in the build context is a key in the image history.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/secrets.toml
